## 3. Suggested Monorepo Directory Structure

A well-organized directory structure is paramount for monorepo maintainability. We will adopt a standard, logical structure that separates applications, reusable packages, tools, and documentation. This structure promotes clear ownership, consistent navigation, and efficient monorepo tooling (e.g., Nx, Turborepo).

```
├── .github/                     # GitHub Actions workflows, issue templates, PR templates
├── apps/                        # Top-level deployable applications, services, or large systems
│   ├── aether-forge/            # The AetherForge application
│   │   └── src/                 # Application code
│   ├── darlek-caan/             # The main Darlek-Caan ecosystem (might contain sub-apps/services)
│   │   ├── api/                 # Main API service
│   │   ├── evolution-sim-engine/ # The ai_evo_sim application
│   │   ├── nbody-simulator/     # The nbody_gravitational_simulator application/service
│   │   ├── chess-engine/        # DARLEK-CAAN-vs-JESUS-CHESS
│   │   └── ui/                  # Any user interface component
│   ├── grog-agi/                # The GROG-The-First-Learning-AGI application
│   │   └── src/
│   ├── huxley/                  # The main Huxley ecosystem (might contain sub-apps/services)
│   │   ├── kernel/              # AGI-KERNEL-
│   │   ├── ethical-reasoning/   # Huxley-A-Reasoning-Framework-for-Ethical-AI
│   │   ├── singularity-loop/    # Huxley-Singularity-Loop-Main
│   │   ├── dna-regulator/       # DNA-Based-Regulator-Core
│   │   ├── echo-chamber/        # echo-chamber-v7
│   │   ├── euler-engine/        # EULER-ENGINE (if an app/service)
│   │   ├── emg-core/            # EMG-CORE (if an app/service specific to Huxley)
